["```javascript
async function traverseDOMAndFetchMetadata(selector, testFunction, apiEndpoint) {
  const matchedElements = [];

  // Helper function to fetch metadata from external API
  async function fetchMetadata(elementId) {
    try {
      const response = await fetch(`${apiEndpoint}/${elementId}`);
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Network response was not ok');
      return await response.json();
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`Failed to fetch metadata for element ${elementId}:`, error);
      return null;
    }
  }

  // Recursive function to traverse the DOM
  async function traverse(node) {
    if (!node) return;

    // Check if the node matches the selector and test function
    if (node.matches(selector) && testFunction(node)) {
      const metadata = await fetchMetadata(node.id);
      if (metadata) matchedElements.push({ element: node, metadata });
    }

    // Recursively traverse child nodes
    for (let i = 0; i < node.children.length; i++) {
      await traverse(node.children[i]);
    }
  }

  // Start traversal from the document body
  await traverse(document.body);

  return matchedElements;
}
```

This code defines an asynchronous function `traverseDOMAndFetchMetadata` that takes a selector, a test function, and an API endpoint as arguments. It uses recursion to traverse the DOM tree starting from the document body, checking each element against the provided selector and test function. If an element matches, it fetches additional metadata using the external API and stores the element along with its metadata in an array.

The `fetchMetadata` helper function handles network requests to the external API, including error handling for connectivity issues. It returns the fetched metadata or null if the request fails.

By using recursion and asynchronous operations, this code efficiently traverses large DOM trees while minimizing the number of network requests. It also gracefully handles edge cases such as missing attributes, temporary disconnection from the external service, and changes in the DOM structure over time."]

['```java
// Java code block for processing log file

import java.util.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.time.*;

public class LogProcessor {
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<String, EventData> eventMap = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public static void processLogFile(String filePath) throws IOException {
        try (BufferedReader reader = Files.newBufferedReader(Paths.get(filePath))) {
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                String[] parts = line.split(",");
                if (parts.length >= 3) {
                    String timestamp = parts[0];
                    String eventId = parts[1];
                    long processingTime = Long.parseLong(parts[2]);
                    LocalDate date = LocalDate.parse(timestamp.split(" ")[0]);

                    eventMap.computeIfAbsent(date.toString(), k -> new EventData()).addEvent(eventId, processingTime);
                }
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("Error reading log file: " + e.getMessage());
        }

        for (Map.Entry<String, EventData> entry : eventMap.entrySet()) {
            String date = entry.getKey();
            EventData data = entry.getValue();
            Map<String, Double> averages = data.calculateAverages();
            System.out.println("Date: " + date + ", Averages: " + averages);
        }
    }

    private static class EventData {
        private final Map<String, List<Long>> eventTimes;

        public EventData() {
            this.eventTimes = new HashMap<>();
        }

        public void addEvent(String eventId, long processingTime) {
            eventTimes.computeIfAbsent(eventId, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(processingTime);
        }

        public Map<String, Double> calculateAverages() {
            Map<String, Double> averages = new HashMap<>();
            for (Map.Entry<String, List<Long>> entry : eventTimes.entrySet()) {
                String eventId = entry.getKey();
                List<Long> times = entry.getValue();
                double average = times.stream().mapToLong(Long::longValue).average().orElse(0.0);
                averages.put(eventId, average);
            }
            return averages;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            processLogFile("path/to/logfile.log");
        } catch (IOException e) {
            System.err.println("Error processing log file: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
